One more important change

You currently have two matrix entries with:

RHEL_MAJOR: "10"

That means both publish to the same destination:

ubi10-init-satellite

The regular UBI 10 init image and the Python 3.12 minimal image will overwrite or race against each other on tags such as:

latest
pipeline-...
sha-...

You need a separate output repository name for the Python image.

Change the script from:

IMAGE_REPOSITORY="${CI_REGISTRY_IMAGE}/ubi${RHEL_MAJOR}-init-satellite"

to:

IMAGE_REPOSITORY="${CI_REGISTRY_IMAGE}/${OUTPUT_IMAGE_NAME}"

Then define the matrix like this:

build_satellite_images:
  extends: .build_satellite_image
  parallel:
    matrix:
      - RHEL_MAJOR: "7"
        OUTPUT_IMAGE_NAME: "ubi7-init-satellite"
        BASE_IMAGE: "registry.gitlab.us.lmco.com/lit/containers/images/base-images/ubi7-init:latest"
      - RHEL_MAJOR: "8"
        OUTPUT_IMAGE_NAME: "ubi8-init-satellite"
        BASE_IMAGE: "registry.gitlab.us.lmco.com/lit/containers/images/base-images/ubi8-init:latest"
      - RHEL_MAJOR: "9"
        OUTPUT_IMAGE_NAME: "ubi9-init-satellite"
        BASE_IMAGE: "registry.gitlab.us.lmco.com/lit/containers/images/base-images/ubi9-init:latest"
      - RHEL_MAJOR: "10"
        OUTPUT_IMAGE_NAME: "ubi10-init-satellite"
        BASE_IMAGE: "registry.gitlab.us.lmco.com/lit/containers/images/base-images/ubi10-init:latest"
      - RHEL_MAJOR: "10"
        OUTPUT_IMAGE_NAME: "ubi10-python3.12-satellite"
        BASE_IMAGE: "registry.gitlab.us.lmco.com/lit/containers/images/base-images/ubi10-python3.12:20260724"

That will publish the new image separately as:

image-builder/ubi10-python3.12-satellite:latest

So the immediate build fix is microdnf; the destination-name fix prevents the Python image from colliding with your existing UBI 10 init image.